and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3F+\\frac{1}{2}G & =3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot 1 & 3\\cdot 3 \\\\ 3\\cdot (-2) & 3\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 \\\\ -6 & 6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3+1 & 9+0 \\\\ -6+2 & 6+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We multiply each entry of $F$ by $3$ and each entry of $G$ by $\\frac{1}{2},$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3F+\\frac{1}{2}G & =3\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\cdot 1 & 3\\cdot 3 \\\\ 3\\cdot (-2) & 3\\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 \\\\ -6 & 6\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3+1 & 9+0 \\\\ -6+2 & 6+3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186250432 :question/problem "Which of the following are square matrices?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 0.5 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}1.5 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0.2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\,\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." "Which of the following are square matrices?\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 0.5 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,S=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,T=\\begin{bmatrix}1.5 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0.2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\,\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186250441 :question/problem "Which of the following best describes the following matrix $A?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "Which of the following best describes the following matrix $A?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186250463 :question/problem "Find $ST$,  if  $S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $T=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" "Find $ST$,  if  $S=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $T=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186250463 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ST & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3+0+8 & 2+0-4 & 3+0+4 \\\\ 0-5+4 & 0+5-2 & 0-0+2 \\\\ 6+0+4 & 4-0-2 & 6+0+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ST & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3+0+8 & 2+0-4 & 3+0+4 \\\\ 0-5+4 & 0+5-2 & 0-0+2 \\\\ 6+0+4 & 4-0-2 & 6+0+2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186250474 :question/problem "Find $MN$, if  $M=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $N=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]=$" "Find $MN$, if  $M=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $N=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=$"] [:db/cas 17592186250474 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}MN & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2+0+4 & 4+0+2 & 6+0+4 \\\\ 0-0+4 & 0-1+2 & 0-0+4 \\\\ 1+0+4 & 2+0+2 & 3+0+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}MN & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2+0+4 & 4+0+2 & 6+0+4 \\\\ 0-0+4 & 0-1+2 & 0-0+4 \\\\ 1+0+4 & 2+0+2 & 3+0+4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186250583 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186250605 :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" "x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186250647 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186250660 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186250703 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186250728 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186250733 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186250760 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186250785 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186250804 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{5}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{5}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186250828 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{10}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{10}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186250929 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{10}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{10}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186251039 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186251073 :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" "x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186251174 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186251368 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186251538 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186251664 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186251693 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186251888 :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" "x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186252381 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186252447 :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" "x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186252503 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186252661 :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" "x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186252743 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186253256 :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,C=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AB=BA={I}_{3}$\n- **II.** $AC=CA={I}_{3}$\n- **III.** $B={A}^{-1}$" "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AB=BA={I}_{3}$\n- **II.** $AC=CA={I}_{3}$\n- **III.** $B={A}^{-1}$"] [:db/cas 17592186253256 :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true. \nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true. \nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."] [:db/cas 17592186253257 :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AC=CA={I}_{3}$\n- **II.** $AD=DA={I}_{3}$\n- **III.** $D={A}^{-1}$" "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AC=CA={I}_{3}$\n- **II.** $AD=DA={I}_{3}$\n- **III.** $D={A}^{-1}$"] [:db/cas 17592186253257 :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AD=DA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AD & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 7 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false. As a result, $D\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." "- First, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AD=DA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AD & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 7 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end